# Trailing whitespace: fatal for an integer, part of the value for a path.
-- options --
mydumper-version: v0.19.3-3
-- input.cnf.esc --
[mydumper]\nthreads=4 \noutputdir=/backup\t\nroutines=1 \n
-- diagnostics --
2:10-2:11 error MDL302[trailing-whitespace-in-value] the value of `threads` ends with whitespace, which GLib keeps
  = mydumper aborts at startup: "option parsing failed: Cannot parse integer value “4 ” for --threads, try --help".
  fix (unsafe): Remove the trailing whitespace
3:18-3:19 error MDL302[trailing-whitespace-in-value] the value of `outputdir` ends with whitespace, which GLib keeps
  = The whitespace becomes part of the value.
  fix (unsafe): Remove the trailing whitespace
-- fixed-unsafe.cnf.esc --
[mydumper]\nthreads=4\noutputdir=/backup\nroutines=1 \n
